{
  // CI dependency-audit gate (replaces `npm audit --production --audit-level=high`).
  // Fails on NEW high/critical advisories in production deps; known-stuck advisories
  // with no non-breaking fix are allowlisted below WITH their exit plan. Don't add
  // to the allowlist without a documented reason + removal trigger.
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "high": true,
  "skip-dev": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // turbo-stream <3.0.0 — REMOVED 2026-06-14 with the React Router 7 migration.
    // RR7 (>=7.17) vendors a patched turbo-stream internally and no longer has an
    // external `turbo-stream` dependency, so the advisory no longer fires.
    // `npm ls turbo-stream` → empty. audit-ci confirmed: "Consider not allowlisting
    // advisory: GHSA-rxv8-25v2-qmq8".
    //
    // esbuild >=0.17 <0.28.1 — RCE via NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY in esbuild's DENO
    // installer (published 2026-06-12). Not applicable: this repo never installs
    // esbuild via Deno; the npm install path is unaffected. esbuild is still in the
    // prod tree because @react-router/dev (a `dependencies` entry — the Dockerfile
    // runs `npm ci --omit=dev` THEN `react-router build`, so the build toolchain must
    // ship in the prod image) pulls vite -> esbuild@0.25.x. It is a build-time-only
    // binary, never invoked at runtime. REMOVE this entry once vite/@react-router/dev
    // resolve esbuild >=0.28.1.
    "GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr",
    //
    // react-router 6.0.0–8.2.0 advisory batch (published ~2026-08-06, CI-red since).
    // Fixed only in RR >=8.2.1 — a MAJOR upgrade this repo must canary-deploy as a
    // dedicated task (the SSR dist/development redirect + ssr.noExternal machinery in
    // vite.config.ts is 7.17-specific; see CLAUDE.md react-router gotcha). Per-advisory
    // applicability (2026-08-07 review):
    //  - GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 (high, RSC CSRF) + GHSA-h8fp-f39c-q6mh (RSC XSS): NOT
    //    APPLICABLE — this app does not use RSC mode.
    //  - GHSA-wrjc-x8rr-h8h6 (open redirect via backslash): admin-only surface behind
    //    Shopify auth; no user-controlled navigation paths.
    //  - GHSA-337j-9hxr-rhxg (deserializeErrors constructor injection): SSR hydration
    //    of the embedded admin only; not reachable from the storefront widget.
    //  - GHSA-chx6-hx7r-mcp5 (high, unauthenticated DoS via route matching): the one
    //    real exposure (Fly hostname is reachable); impact bounded to CPU exhaustion +
    //    health-check restart on a rate-limited, auto-restarting app. Accepted until
    //    the upgrade.
    // REMOVAL TRIGGER: the react-router >=8.2.1 migration (canary-deploy, re-verify the
    // ssr.noExternal guard). Remove all five entries in that PR.
    "GHSA-wrjc-x8rr-h8h6",
    "GHSA-h8fp-f39c-q6mh",
    "GHSA-337j-9hxr-rhxg",
    "GHSA-chx6-hx7r-mcp5",
    "GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2"
  ]
}
